---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site";

const updated = "August 3, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Learn how Toolsiva handles browser-processed input, technical logs, cookies, analytics, advertising and privacy requests."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:py-16">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-brand-300">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-500">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-brand-400/20 bg-brand-500/[0.06] p-5 text-sm leading-7 text-zinc-300">
      Toolsiva is designed around browser-first processing. Most tool content stays on your
      device unless a page clearly explains otherwise.
    </div>

    <div class="prose-premium mt-10 space-y-10 text-sm leading-7 text-zinc-300">
      <section>
        <h2>1. Scope of this policy</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy describes how Toolsiva handles information when you visit the
          website, use its tools or contact us. It applies to pages operated under the Toolsiva
          domain and does not control third-party websites linked from the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Information processed inside your browser</h2>
        <p>
          Text, code, credentials, QR payloads, calculator values and conversion inputs are
          generally processed locally by browser-side code. Unless a tool clearly states
          otherwise, Toolsiva does not intentionally upload that content to an application
          server for processing or storage.
        </p>
        <p>
          Browser-first processing does not remove every risk. Your device, browser extensions,
          network environment or copied output may expose information. Avoid entering secrets
          unless the tool and your environment are appropriate for that purpose.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Information collected automatically</h2>
        <p>
          Hosting, content-delivery and security providers may process technical information
          needed to deliver and protect the website. This can include an IP address, approximate
          region, browser and device type, requested page, referral information, timestamps,
          performance measurements and suspected abuse events.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Local storage and browser features</h2>
        <p>
          Individual tools may use temporary browser memory, canvas, clipboard, download or other
          browser capabilities to perform a requested action. Toolsiva does not currently require
          a user account. Any future persistent preference storage will be documented where it is
          used.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Cookies and consent</h2>
        <p>
          Essential infrastructure may use limited cookies or similar technologies for security,
          traffic management and service delivery. Toolsiva also offers an analytics preference
          banner for optional Google Analytics storage. Analytics storage is denied by default and
          is enabled only after you select “Accept analytics.”
        </p>
        <p>
          Your selection is stored in your browser so the website can remember it. You can review
          or change that selection at any time through the “Cookie settings” link in the footer.
          Rejecting optional analytics does not prevent access to Toolsiva’s tools.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Google Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Toolsiva uses Google Analytics 4 to understand general website usage, such as visited
          pages, approximate location, browser and device information, referral source, session
          timing and broad interaction events. Google may process this information on Toolsiva’s
          behalf under Google’s applicable terms and privacy documentation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Toolsiva configures Google Consent Mode v2 with analytics storage denied by default.
          Advertising storage, advertising user data and advertising personalization remain
          denied. Google Signals and advertising-personalization signals are disabled in the
          website tag.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tool inputs, passwords, tokens, QR payloads and generated results are not intentionally
          included in analytics events. Toolsiva does not currently display third-party
          advertising. This policy will be updated before introducing advertising technologies
          that materially change how information is processed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Contact messages</h2>
        <p>
          When you contact Toolsiva by email, your email provider and our email provider process
          the address, message content, attachments and related delivery metadata. Contact
          messages may be retained while responding, resolving a reported issue and maintaining
          reasonable records.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Service providers and disclosures</h2>
        <p>
          Toolsiva may rely on hosting, domain, content-delivery, security, email and analytics
          providers. Information may also be disclosed when reasonably necessary to comply with
          law, protect users, investigate abuse, enforce terms or preserve the security and
          integrity of the service.
        </p>
        <p>Toolsiva does not sell personal information.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          Tool content processed only in the browser is not intentionally retained by Toolsiva.
          Infrastructure logs and contact records may be retained for limited periods based on
          security, operational, support and legal needs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>10. International processing</h2>
        <p>
          Infrastructure providers may operate in multiple countries. As a result, technical or
          contact information may be processed outside your location under the safeguards and
          terms applied by those providers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>11. Security</h2>
        <p>
          Reasonable technical and organizational measures are used to protect the service, but
          no internet system is guaranteed to be completely secure. You remain responsible for
          protecting your device, browser, copied results and any sensitive content.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>12. Children</h2>
        <p>
          Toolsiva is a general-audience utility website and is not directed to children below
          the age required for independent consent in their jurisdiction. Do not knowingly submit
          personal information about a child through contact channels.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>13. Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>
          You may stop using the service, clear browser data, restrict optional storage and
          manage browser or device permissions. Privacy rights differ by jurisdiction and may
          include access, correction, deletion, objection or restriction rights.
        </p>
        <p>
          Requests may be sent to{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.
          We may need sufficient information to verify and process a request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>14. Policy updates</h2>
        <p>
          This policy may change as Toolsiva introduces new features, infrastructure, analytics
          or advertising. Material revisions will be reflected by the date shown at the top of
          this page.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
